7:- [x] **1. Low, long horizontal house**, 22 x 18, walls y=1..5, roof to y=7. Part 1 shell. Vocab `stucco_wall`, `header_course`.
8:- [ ] **2. Very low-pitch gable roof, deep eaves**: hand-built stepped slab roof, ridge along x at z=16..17 (y=7), eaves z=6/27 (y=6), 2-cell overhang front and back, 1 at the gable ends; dark_oak_slab fascia ring. Part 3. Vocab `roof_band`, `fascia_ring`.
9:- [ ] **3. Exposed beam ends**: dark_oak_log axis z at y=5 on x=10,13,...,31, running z=5..28 (3 cells beyond the walls on each side). Part 3. Vocab `beam_line`.
10:- [ ] **4. Post-and-beam structure**: dark_oak_log posts (vertical, y=2..4) on every beam line of the south wall, the 4 house corners, the ring corners. Beams above carry the roof. Part 4. Vocab `post`.
11:- [ ] **5. Flat carport roof stepping one level below the main eave**: smooth_stone_slab deck at y=5, x=0..9, z=7..21, dark_oak_slab fascia on x=0, z=7, z=21; on dark_oak_log posts (x=1; z=8,14,20; y=1..4) and beams (y=4). Part 2. Vocab `carport`.
12:- [ ] **6. Carport breeze-block screen** at z=21, x=1..9, y=1..4: checkerboard of white_concrete and AIR (holes left open). Part 2. Vocab `breeze_screen`.
15:- [x] **7. Mostly blank white stucco** x=10..17 and x=21..31, y=2..4, white_concrete on a smooth_stone base (y=1) and a dark_oak_planks header (y=5). Part 1 (walls), part 4 (glazing). Vocab `stucco_wall`.
16:- [ ] **8. Clerestory strip** at y=4, z=8: glass_pane x=22..24, 26..27, 29..30 with dark_oak_log mullions at x=25 and x=28. Part 4. Vocab `clerestory`.
17:- [ ] **9. Stone feature wall** freestanding at z=7, x=11..17, y=1..4: mud_bricks with ~25% packed_mud (seeded), mud_brick_slab cap at y=5 on x=11,12,14,15,17 only. Part 4. Vocab `ledgestone_wall`.
18:- [ ] **10. Bold orange front door**: entry recess x=18..20 z=8 (air), door wall at z=9: orange_concrete panels x=18 and x=20 y=2..4; acacia_door at x=19 z=9 y=2..3 (facing north); orange_concrete transom (19,4,9); smooth_stone reveal x=17, white_concrete reveal x=21. Part 1 leaves the niche, part 4 fills it. Vocab `orange_entry`.
19:- [ ] **11. Entry landing and stepping-pad path** (x=18..20, z=6..7 landing; pads z=1,3,5 in sand). Part 2. Vocab `stepping_pad`.
22:- [ ] **12. Floor-to-ceiling glass wall with thin dark posts**: glass_pane y=2..4 between dark_oak_log posts on every beam line x=10..31; only base (y=1) and header (y=5) stay opaque. Part 4. Vocab `glass_bay`, `post`.
23:- [ ] **13. Three sliding-door gaps** x=14..15, x=20..21, x=26..27 at z=25 (y=2..3 AIR, glass_pane at y=4 above). Part 1 leaves them, part 4 glazes y=4. Vocab `slider_gap`.
24:- [ ] **14. Gable-end glass clerestories** x=10 and x=31, y=6, z=14..19. Part 3 (roof) places the panes. Vocab `glass_bay`.
25:- [ ] **15. West and east windows**: dining x=10 z=14..16 y=3..4; bedroom 1 x=31 z=10..12 y=3..4; bath clerestory x=31 z=15..16 y=4; master full-height x=31 z=21..23 y=2..4; utility door gap x=10 z=10 y=2..3 (with an open dark_oak_door). Part 4. Vocab `glass_bay`, `utility_door`.
28:- [ ] **16. Open-sky courtyard** x=17..21, z=12..17, no roof and no slab (dirt at y=0): glass_pane ring (x=16, x=22, z=11, z=18, y=2..4), dark_oak_log posts at the 4 corners and on x=19 at z=11, z=18 (y=4 only above the doors), dark_oak_planks header y=5, ring crossing band C glazed at y=6. Part 1 (header, openings), part 4 (glass, posts). Vocab `atrium_ring`.
29:- [ ] **17. Atrium planting**: the atrium's interior designer (a small tree-fern garden: grass_block patch, a potted palm, large_fern, rocks, a smooth_stone stepping path between the two doors at x=19..20). Room "atrium".
32:- [ ] **18. Concrete driveway** x=1..8, z=1..21, smooth_stone with light_gray_concrete joint rows at z=4,8,12,16. Part 2. Vocab `joint_row`.
33:- [ ] **19. Sidewalk** z=0 x=0..33 smooth_stone. Part 2.
34:- [ ] **20. Two-tone 1950s car** parked nose to the street on the driveway, x=3..5, y=1..2, z=1..7: cyan_concrete body, white roof and tail fins, glass cabin, iron_block chrome bumpers, black_concrete tyres, yellow_concrete headlamps, red_concrete tail lamps. Part 5. Vocab `car_50s`.
35:- [ ] **21. Desert planting out front**: sand yard with gravel beds (x=22..30 and x=10..16, z=1..5), cactus cluster (x=23..29, z=2..4; sand under each cactus), two palms (12,3) and (30,4). Part 5. Vocab `palm`, `saguaro`, `barrel_cactus`.
36:- [ ] **22. Low mailbox** at (9,1): dark_oak_fence post y=1, box y=2. Part 5. Vocab `mailbox`.
37:- [ ] **23. Kidney-shaped pool** (RESERVED cells in plan.md): water y=-1..0, light_blue_concrete liner (floor y=-2, walls y=-1), smooth_quartz_slab coping at y=0 round the rim. Part 6. Vocab `kidney_pool`.
38:- [ ] **24. Back patio and pool deck** smooth_stone y=0 (patio x=10..31 z=26..28; deck x=11..24 z=29..33); loungers and a parasol table on the patio; a palm at (29,31). Part 2 (paving), part 6 (furniture, palm). Vocab `lounger`, `patio_table`.
39:- [ ] **25. Lawns** grass_block y=0, x=0..10 and x=25..33 z=26..33 where not paved; side strips of sand. Part 2.
40:- [ ] **26. Outdoor lighting**: two `garden_lamp` posts flanking the entry path at (17,0..,5) and (21,0..,5) on sand, plus 2 more by the pool; `garden_lamp`. Part 6.
43:- [ ] **27. Open-plan living room** with **sunken conversation pit** (x=13..17, z=20..23, floor y=0 smooth_quartz, steps and built-in benches, low table) and **freestanding fireplace** (x=20..21, z=21..22 y=1..8; shaft by part 3). Rooms "living". Vocab `conversation_pit`, `fireplace_stack`, `sofa_low`, `egg_chair`.
44:- [ ] **28. Dining area** with a table and six chairs, a sideboard, pendant lamp. Room "dining". Vocab `dining_set`, `sideboard`.
45:- [ ] **29. Galley kitchen with breakfast bar**. Room "kitchen". Vocab `galley_kitchen`, `bar_stool`.
46:- [ ] **30. Entry gallery** with a bench and a coat hook wall. Room "gallery".
47:- [ ] **31. Corridor to three bedrooms**: bedroom 1, bedroom 2, master. Beds, wardrobes, nightstands. Vocab `bed_double`, `wardrobe`, `nightstand`.
48:- [ ] **32. Two bathrooms**. Vocab `bath_fit`.
49:- [ ] **33. Warm wood panelling** (spruce_planks ceiling, spruce_trapdoor wall panelling), **terrazzo floors** (smooth_stone + light_gray/white flecks) in the public rooms. Vocab `terrazzo_floor`, `panel_wall`.
50:- [ ] **34. Period furniture**: low sofas, egg chair, sideboard, tulip side table, floor lamp. Vocab above.
51:- [ ] **35. Lit**: every room has a hung lantern or sea_lantern light. Vocab `hung_lantern`.
